title: "thread under a Herdr parent: where its new session runs (S2)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Herdr
    lg1: Tmux
    lg2: None
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 tan
  class lg2 blue
  s0: Legacy row, no tmux session
  s1: No session row
  s2: Herdr row Pending, no pane yet
  s3: tmux session running
  s4: tmux session idle
  s5: Herdr pane bound, first input waiting
  s6: Herdr pane made, location not recorded
  s7: Herdr execution retired
  s8: Herdr pane running
  s9: Row deleted by thread_gc
  s10: Herdr pane idle
  [*] --> s0
  [*] --> s1
  s0 --> s2: a queued input starts the thread's session (turn host judges the host)
  s1 --> s2: a queued input starts the thread's session (turn host judges the host)
  s0 --> s3: a queued input starts the session on tmux
  s1 --> s3: a queued input starts the session on tmux
  s2 --> s5: Herdr creates the pane (answer may be lost)
  s2 --> s6: Herdr creates the pane (answer may be lost)
  s3 --> s4: the turn ends and the thread stays idle past an hour
  s2 --> s7: unplaced row resolved: the pane adopted, or the row retired
  s4 --> s0: idle cleanup ends the session
  s5 --> s8: the first input is submitted to the Herdr pane
  s6 --> s5: unplaced row resolved: the pane adopted, or the row retired
  s7 --> s2: a queued input starts the thread's session (turn host judges the host)
  s0 --> s9: thread_gc deletes the row
  s8 --> s10: the turn ends and the thread stays idle past an hour
  s10 --> s7: idle cleanup ends the session
  s7 --> s9: thread_gc deletes the row
